description.narrative:
The project aims to improve the technical platform of the Simao Mendes hospital in order to improve access to quality health services for the population of Guinea Bissau. Specifically, the project aims to:
- the reduction of mortality linked to kidney failure by ensuring access to the necessary care through the rehabilitation and equipment of the hemodialysis center;
- improving the population's access to drugs by supporting the rehabilitation of the Bissau drug warehouse;
- improvement of the country's treatment capacities through the rehabilitation of the laboratory and the blood bank;
- the strengthening of the country's medical capacities through the purchase of medical and non-medical equipment for the benefit of the Hospital;
- capacity building in the maintenance of infrastructure and equipment delivered.
